  "body": "# simpler doctype declaration\r\nOne of my favorite things about HTML5 vs. XHTML is using this in your websites: `<!DOCTYPE html>` instead of this: \r\n`<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\"\r\n   \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\">`\r\n( I typed the first one in, but copied and pasted the second one)\r\nthis improves\r\n1.  writing ease of writing HTML documents,\r\n2. page download speeds\r\n3. not having to juggle 3 or 4 different declarations depending if you use certain tags\r\nsomething that would be even better would be the `<!d>` tag or the `<!>` tag or something like that.",
